# DiskANN/Vamana build hyperparameters tuned for BIGANN-1B (128-d L2, 1B uint8
# vectors widened to Float32 on ingest).
#
# These trace the DiskANN paper (NeurIPS '19) Table 4 BIGANN-1B configuration:
#   R=128, L=200, alpha=1.2, PQ chunks=32 -> Recall@10 ~= 0.95
# with a small RAM headroom bump (paper: 64 GB; we have 223 GB).
#
# Sizing rationale (vs build_paper.env which targets SIFT-1M):
#   - max_degree 96 -> 128: at 1B points the 1-NN ball gets dense enough that
#     a 96-edge graph stalls during traversal; the DiskANN paper switches to
#     128 starting at 100M.
#   - build_search_list_size 200 -> 200 (kept): paper value. Higher L raises
#     graph quality but build time grows roughly linearly; not worth it for
#     the small Recall@10 delta.
#   - alpha 1.4 -> 1.2: paper's recommendation for L2 at billion scale.
#     alpha=1.4 prunes too aggressively — graph diameter blows up on 1B nodes.
#   - pq_chunks 16 -> 32: 1B * pq_chunks bytes of PQ codebook RAM; 32 GB of
#     codebook (vs 16 GB) gives noticeably better PQ approximation, which
#     dominates per-hop candidate ranking on a 1B disk graph.
#   - num_threads 64: build is roughly embarrassingly parallel per shard.
#   - build_ram_limit_gb 8 -> 128: PQ codebook (32 GB) + in-memory shard
#     graph (~30-60 GB during merge) + headroom. Paper used 64 GB; we have
#     more, so we use it.
#
# Expected wall-clock on 64 cores / NVMe RAID: ~4-6 days. DiskANN paper
# reports 5 days on a similar machine. Pair with --build-timeout 168h (7d)
# in run_bigann.sh.

MAX_DEGREE=128
BUILD_SEARCH_LIST_SIZE=200
ALPHA=1.2
PQ_CHUNKS=32

NUM_THREADS=64
BUILD_RAM_LIMIT_GB=128

HASH_SEED=42
